      *
      *A whole ILE COBOL program: an order register that reads a file,
      *totals by customer, and prints. Every division appears, in the
      *order the compiler requires.
      *
      *Member: ORDREG   Compilable: complete program, but not built; the
      *        files it names are not defined here (CRTBNDCBL)
      *Source: ILE COBOL Language Reference SC09-2539.
      *Retrieved: 2026-07-29
      *
       PROCESS NOMONOPRC OPTIONS.
      *
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. ORDREG.
       AUTHOR. EXAMPLE LTD.
      *
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. IBM-ISERIES.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. IBM-ISERIES.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.
           CURRENCY SIGN IS "$".
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT ORDER-FILE ASSIGN TO DATABASE-ORDHDR
             ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
             ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
             RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
             FILE STATUS IS WS-STATUS.
           SELECT PRINT-FILE ASSIGN TO PRINTER-QPRINT.
      *
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  ORDER-FILE.
       01  ORDER-RECORD.
               COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF ORDHDR.
       FD  PRINT-FILE.
       01  PRINT-RECORD              PIC X(132).
      *
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       77  WS-STATUS                 PIC XX.
           88  END-OF-FILE           VALUE "10".
       01  WS-TOTALS.
               05  WS-CUST-TOTAL     PIC S9(9)V99 PACKED-DECIMAL.
               05  WS-GRAND-TOTAL    PIC S9(11)V99 PACKED-DECIMAL.
               05  WS-COUNT          PIC 9(7) BINARY VALUE ZERO.
       01  WS-HEADING.
               05  FILLER        PIC X(14) VALUE "ORDER REGISTER".
               05  WS-RUN-DATE   PIC X(10).
       01  WS-WHEN                   PIC X(21).
       66  WS-ALL-TOTALS RENAMES WS-CUST-TOTAL THRU WS-GRAND-TOTAL.
      *
       LINKAGE SECTION.
       01  LK-COMPANY                PIC X(3).
      *
       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LK-COMPANY.
       MAIN-LINE.
               PERFORM INITIALIZE-RUN
               PERFORM PROCESS-ORDERS UNTIL END-OF-FILE
               PERFORM PRINT-TOTALS
               GOBACK.
      *
       INITIALIZE-RUN.
               OPEN INPUT ORDER-FILE
                    OUTPUT PRINT-FILE
               MOVE WHEN-COMPILED TO WS-WHEN
               MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE (1:10) TO WS-RUN-DATE
               INITIALIZE WS-TOTALS                                     reset
               READ ORDER-FILE
                 AT END SET END-OF-FILE TO TRUE
               END-READ.
      *
      *The register itself. EVALUATE picks the handling, and the
      *arithmetic carries ON SIZE ERROR for the total overflowing.
       PROCESS-ORDERS.
               EVALUATE TRUE
                 WHEN ORDSTS = "X"
                   CONTINUE                                             skip
                 WHEN ORDAMT > 0
                   ADD ORDAMT TO WS-CUST-TOTAL
                     ON SIZE ERROR
                       DISPLAY "total overflow" UPON SYSOUT
                   END-ADD
                   ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
                 WHEN OTHER
                   SUBTRACT ORDAMT FROM WS-CUST-TOTAL
               END-EVALUATE
               COMPUTE WS-GRAND-TOTAL = WS-GRAND-TOTAL
                   + FUNCTION MAX(ORDAMT 0)
               READ ORDER-FILE
                 AT END SET END-OF-FILE TO TRUE
               END-READ.
      *
      *A literal continued onto the next line: the hyphen indicator
      *resumes it, and the first nonblank character is the quote.
       PRINT-TOTALS.
               MOVE SPACES TO PRINT-RECORD
               STRING "Orders: " DELIMITED BY SIZE
                      WS-COUNT DELIMITED BY SIZE
                      INTO PRINT-RECORD
               END-STRING
               WRITE PRINT-RECORD AFTER ADVANCING PAGE
               DISPLAY "register complete for a very long messag
      -    "e indeed" UPON SYSOUT
      D        DISPLAY "debug only" UPON SYSOUT
               CLOSE ORDER-FILE PRINT-FILE
               MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE.
      *
      *Conditional compilation, an IBM extension: a compilation
      *variable is defined and the lines to compile chosen by it.
           >>DEFINE DEBUG AS B"1"
           >>IF DEBUG IS DEFINED
               DISPLAY "debug build" UPON SYSOUT
           >>ELSE
               CONTINUE
           >>END-IF
           >>EVALUATE TRUE
           >>WHEN DEBUG IS DEFINED
               DISPLAY "still debug" UPON SYSOUT
           >>END-EVALUATE
      *
       END PROGRAM ORDREG.
